  <p>68. For section 133 of the principal Act, the following section shall be substituted, namely:-</p>
  <p>"133. Any country, which is a signatory or party or a group of countries, union of countries or inter-governmental organisations which are signatories or parties to an international, regional or bi-Iateral treaty, convention or arrangement to which India is also a signatory or party and which affords to the applicants for patents in India or to citizens of India similar privileges as are granted to their own citizens or citizens to their member countries in respect of the grant of patents and protection of patent rights shall be a convention country or convention countries for the purposes ofthis Act.".</p>
  <p>69. In section 135 ofthe principal Act, after sub-section (2), the following sub-section shall be inserted, namely:-</p>
  <p>"(3) In case of an application filed under the Patent Cooperation Treaty designating India and clairrring priority from a previously filed application in India, the provisions of sub-sections (1) and (2) shall apply as ifthe previously filed application were the basic application:</p>
  <p>Provided that a request for examination under section lIB shall be made only for one ofthe applications filed in India.".</p>
